{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109084","id":2704444318,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6hMoue","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109084","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109084.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109084.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109084","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109084/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109084/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109084/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/bd9d1bf070fc054c81477cc03a74e600cf4cf641","number":109084,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add material debanding for use in Mobile rendering method.","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR is a trimmed down and slightly modified version of @Calinou's #87350 -- Calinou should take most of the credit for this!\r\n\r\nThis PR adds a new `RenderingServer.material_use_debanding` property that is configured at project startup by the existing `rendering/anti_aliasing/quality/use_debanding` project setting. This `RenderingServer` property can also be toggled at runtime. This new debanding mode only functions with the Mobile rendering method, but can be extended to the Compatibility rendering method in the future.\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7336\r\n- Closes the Mobile renderer part of https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/4193\r\n\r\n## Screenshots (view at 100% size for correct appearance)\r\n\r\n| | Material Debanding Off | Material Debanding On\r\n| -- | -- | --\r\nViewport Debanding Off | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e179cc38-d579-4175-84e2-f5f23e6b427a\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/02a00336-d4fe-406d-a009-433ba0657087\" />\r\nViewport Debanding On | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/730f68a0-e40c-4b74-a211-77b127f8cfc2\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dbbd3574-aed6-405c-b55e-461ab7cbc360\" />\r\n\r\n| | Material Debanding Off | Material Debanding On\r\n| -- | -- | --\r\nViewport Debanding Off | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/18a4a187-1748-41b5-9f4d-532ab80678fa\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/803ae6ef-0dc7-458a-894e-b2c7ab0ac86e\" />\r\nViewport Debanding On | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/27c6876f-882a-4170-adc1-f7bad6342831\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3d070232-a18f-48cb-95df-c27876e9406c\" />\r\n\r\n## Comparison to original PR\r\n\r\nCompared to [Calinou's original PR](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/87350), I have changed the following:\r\n\r\n- Corrected Mobile material debanding to be applied as the last step before quantization from floating point to integer values and corrected the scale to align to 10-bit integer values\r\n- Disabled material debanding entirely when using the Forward+ or Compatibility rendering method\r\n  - Because Forward+ uses floating point buffers for rendering materials, there is never a need for material debanding\r\n  - It is difficult to get flawless results with the additive lights and the Compatibility rendering method. Calinou did a fantastic job getting close, but I think it is better to explore this in a followup PR instead.\r\n- Consolidated the project setting for `use_debanding` so that it affects both viewport and material debanding\r\n  - Viewport and material debanding can still be individually controlled through scripting\r\n  - I don't see any issue with combining material and viewport debanding on the Mobile rendering method. I think most users would want this behaviour and if they don't, they can turn individual settings on/off at run-time.\r\n- Updated documentation, including a simplified project setting description that simply states that the dithering filter is applied at different steps of the rendering process depending on the rendering method and HDR 2D setting. Details about when viewport/material debanding apply are included in their documentation.\r\n- Added an offset to Mobile material debanding\r\n\r\n## Dither offset\r\n\r\nHere is the tool that I used to determine a good offset for the material debanding: \r\n[dither-offset-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22164047/dither-offset-test.zip)\r\nIn this image the top and bottom bars are the original colour, the left is the base dither pattern, the right is the offset dither pattern, and the middle is the left and right added to each other (in linear space):\r\n<img width=\"639\" height=\"360\" alt=\"468825058-8467669d-97fc-42f1-b414-e2590c6d6252\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6787be30-ed5a-4754-aee5-ee770f29cd70\" />\r\n\r\n## For reviewers\r\n\r\n- This code assumes that mobile materials always render to a 10-bit linear buffer. I have noted this as a comment in the glsl shader. If there is any configuration where this isn't the case, please let me know! (I know this will no longer be the case after #109971 is merged...)\r\n\r\n## Test projects\r\n\r\n- [material_debanding_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22162804/material_debanding_test.zip)\r\n- [test_material_debanding.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22163903/test_material_debanding.zip)","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mj